meta {
  name: Update Channel Settings
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/communication/channel-settings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "isSmsChannelEnabled": false
  }
}

docs {
  Partially update the business's messaging channel capability for the active
  scope. Only supplied flags change; a missing settings row is created with
  defaults (all channels enabled) on first write. Tenant + branch come from the
  JWT — never the body (CLAUDE.md §4.7).

  Setting a flag to `false` suppresses that channel for EVERY automatic
  notification in the scope (business capability gate). Returns the full settings
  view (same shape as **Get Channel Settings**).

  ## Fields (all optional)
  - `isEmailChannelEnabled`, `isSmsChannelEnabled`, `isWhatsappChannelEnabled`.
}
